# Diagrams

Applies when editing markdown, HTML, or `.mmd`/`.mermaid` sources.

1. **Would a paragraph or table do the same job?** If yes, do not draw. Highest-quality move is deletion.
2. **Load** `get_skill("pn-diagram-design")` (or `get_command("pn-diagram")`) before drawing. Follow **`pn-core://reference/diagram-baseline.md`** when MCP is available.
3. **Pick one visual type** and state it. Split above ~9 nodes rather than packing more boxes. Confirm type, size, and planned cuts before drawing.
4. **Mermaid:** include `accTitle` and `accDescr`. **Editorial HTML/SVG:** tokens from `.pncore-design.md` (`paper`, `ink`, `muted`, `accent`, `link`); never default to Geist or template cyan/purple.
5. **Accent** on 1–2 focals only. Static by default.
6. **Ship gate:** emit D-01–D-10 from `pn-core://reference/diagram-baseline.md`. **`DIAGRAM: NO-GO`** → fix before done. `/pn-diagram` also runs skeptic (and `pn-render-verify` on editorial HTML).
